/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig
.DS_Store
*.profraw
/benchmarks/results/local/
node_modules/
firebase-debug.log

# The Node addon is a build artifact.
sdk/node/vdb.node

# Android build artifacts.
sdk/android/src/main/jniLibs/

# iOS build artifacts.
target/xcframework/
sdk/ios/.build/

# Python build artefacts. The bundled shared library is produced per platform at release time
# and must never be committed: it would be one architecture's binary in everyone's checkout.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
sdk/python/dist/
sdk/python/build/
sdk/python/*.egg-info/
sdk/python/isha_vector_db/*.so
sdk/python/isha_vector_db/*.dylib
sdk/python/isha_vector_db/*.dll

# Fuzzing build output, and crashes as the fuzzer drops them. A crash only belongs in the
# repository once it has been promoted to a regression case under fuzz/corpus/.
crates/*/fuzz/target/
crates/*/fuzz/artifacts/

# Node platform packages are filled in by the release workflow.
sdk/node/npm/*/vdb.node

# React Native build artefacts. include/vdb.h is copied from the FFI crate by prepack so the
# tarball is self-contained; committing it would be a second copy of a frozen header, and the
# copy that goes stale is always the one nobody compiles. The native libraries are per-ABI
# binaries assembled at release time.
sdk/react-native/include/
sdk/react-native/android/jniLibs/
sdk/react-native/ios/Vdb.xcframework/
sdk/react-native/*.tgz
